# A-box check: catalogue as yardstick. The characteristics of 351-45 are
# supplied as named individuals and the answer reports, per characteristic,
# whether the case states a value for it. Without a case every one reads as not
# stated, which is what the question asks rather than an answer from the
# pattern.
#
# CQ 24: Which characteristics of the catalogue does a case state a value for,
# and which does it leave open?
#
# Clause 351-45 names the time and quality characteristics a control may be
# described by, and they are supplied as named individuals. A model states a
# value for as many as it cares about.
#
# Listing them would report the same thirteen whatever case is loaded. Holding
# them against the case reports what this control actually specifies, and the
# unstated half is the useful one: a control with no stated dead time carries
# no timing a requirement could be checked against.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?characteristic ?kind ?standing ?quantity ?unit
WHERE {
  ?c a ?kind . ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Characteristic .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Characteristic }
  OPTIONAL {
    ?value iec60050:forCharacteristic ?c .
    OPTIONAL { ?value iec60050:quantity ?quantity }
    OPTIONAL { ?value iec60050:unit     ?unit }
  }
  BIND(IF(BOUND(?value), "stated", "not stated") AS ?standing)
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?c), ".*#", "") AS ?characteristic)
} ORDER BY ?standing ?kind ?characteristic
